(2) "Commercial credit report" means any report provided to a business for a legitimate business purpose, relating to the financial status or payment habits of a business that is the subject of the report. "Commercial credit report" does not include any of the following:

(a) A report prepared for commercial insurance underwriting, claims, or auditing purposes;

(b) A report containing information related to transactions or experiences between the subject and the person making the report;

(c) An authorization or approval of a specific extension of credit directly or indirectly by the issuer of a credit card or similar device;

(d) Any report in which a person that has been requested by a third party to make a specific extension of credit directly or indirectly to the subject conveys its decision with respect to that request.
